{title: 381 - Holy Sabbath Day of Rest}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #381 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 381}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Holy Sabbath day of rest, By our Master richly blest,
[Bb]God created [Eb]and divine, Set aside for holy time.
[Eb]Yes, the holy [Bb7/F]Sabbath [Ab]rest, By our God [Bb]divinely [Eb]blest,
[Ab]It to us a sign shall be [Eb]Throughout all eternity.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb]Yes, the holy Sabbath rest,
[Eb]By our God divinely [Ab]blest,
[Gm]It to [Bb7/F]us [Ab]a sign [Bb]shall be
[Eb]Throughout all eternity.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Seek not pleasures of this earth,
[Bb]With [Eb]its folly, noise, and mirth,
[Eb]There are [Bb7/F]better [Ab]things [Bb]in store,
[Ab]Over on the [Eb]other shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]As the Sabbath draweth on
[Bb]Friday [Eb]eve at set of sun,
[Eb]Christian [Bb7/F]household [Bb]then should [Eb]meet,
[Ab]Sing and pray at [Eb]Jesus'feet.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Asking Him for saving grace,
[Bb]Also [Eb]vict'ry in the race,
[Eb]And to [Bb7/F]help [Ab]us by [Bb]His pow'r,
[Ab]To keep holy [Eb]every hour.
{end_of_verse}
